# VIII10 — M3: the genuine response obeys a quantitative two-sided bound, and `σ₃ ≠ 0`

From M2, `q3_1 ≤ -5/384` on the whole compact window.  Feeding the constant source
`-5/384` into the accepted order reversal `bfun_anti` gives

  `bfun 0 (const (-5/384)) R ≤ cj 1 R`   for every `R > 3`,

and the constant source has the exact closed response `5/(3072 R)`.  The accepted upper bounds
give `cj 1 R ≤ 1/(8R)` and `σ₃(1) ≤ 1/8`; passing `R cj 1 R` to its limit gives
`5/3072 ≤ σ₃(1)`.

General `j ≠ 0` then follows from the accepted scaling `cj j = j³ cj 1`,
`σ₃(j) = j³ σ₃(1)` — not by re-solving, and not by treating `j > 0` only.
-/

